This hypothesis is attractive, and (owing to Davis' 1985 book and the
resulting movie) is popular as well.  But it's not written in stone
just yet.  Anderson's article, "Tetrodotoxin and the zombi
phenomenon" (J. Ethnopharm. 23(1): 121) casts some doubt on the
theory; Davis responds in 25(1), p. 119.  There is also an article
by one W.B. Booth in _Science_ 240:274, entitled "Voodoo science",
with accompanying response by Davis.  The latter exchange I haven't
read.

