  In comparing GP to Darwinian evolution I think you overlook one important
thing -- computation time. It took nature billions of years using
a massively parallel computer ("The computer that came after Deep Thought")
to come up with most of the solutions that are around today. I believe
we can do better by focusing on specific areas but I do not think GP
running on anything less than a TeraOP computer will beat human scientists.
Is there even a GP theorem proving system? I've only seen expert system
driven ones and those aren't really very good.

  How would a GP physicist know when to halt anyway? (especially in
fields like Quantum Gravity where there is no experiment to "test the
fitness") If it were discovering the laws of motion, would it stop
at Newton/Gallileo or go on to Einstein? And after a GP has found
the answer, could we even make sense of its solution?

  


